            <div xml:id="d445">

                <pb facs="0625" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/6069: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-11-05T21:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">November 5,
                                1928—9 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:54
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>American electoral information report number 10. Conservatives 49,666; Liberals
                    67,939. Precincts reported: 362 precincts; unreported, 70.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">La Prensa</hi>, chief Conservative organ, headlines
                    tonight, “The American supervision has honorably observed its promise. The
                    elections Sunday were honest, tranquil, correct, and honorable. The Liberals
                    obtained the victory.”</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">El Comercio</hi>, leading Liberal organ, headlines, “The
                    United States is vindicated before the world.”</p>
                <p>Other comment similarly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
